,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/29","description":"When it rubs the rocks on its neck against you, that's proof of its love for you. However, the rocks are sharp, so the gesture is quite painful!"},{"id":"swsh3.5-3","localId":"3","name":"Kakuna","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/3","description":"While awaiting evolution, it hides from predators under leaves and in nooks of branches."},{"id":"swsh3.5-30","localId":"30","name":"Lycanroc","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/30","description":"The rocks in its mane are sharper than a knife. Fragments that break off are treasured as good luck charms."},{"id":"swsh3.5-31","localId":"31","name":"Rolycoly","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/31","description":"Most of its body has the same composition as coal. Fittingly, this Pokémon was first discovered in coal mines about 400 years ago."},{"id":"swsh3.5-32","localId":"32","name":"Grapploct V","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/32"},{"id":"swsh3.5-33","localId":"33","name":"Ekans","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/33","description":"The eggs of bird Pokémon are its favorite food. It swallows eggs whole, so sometimes an egg gets stuck, and Ekans faints."},{"id":"swsh3.5-34","localId":"34","name":"Arbok","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/34","description":"After stunning its opponents with the pattern on its stomach, it quickly wraps them up in its body and waits for them to stop moving."},{"id":"swsh3.5-35","localId":"35","name":"Galarian Zigzagoon","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/35","description":"Its restlessness has it constantly running around. If it sees another Pokémon, it will purposely run into them in order to start a fight."},{"id":"swsh3.5-36","localId":"36","name":"Galarian Linoone","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/36","description":"It uses its long tongue to taunt opponents. Once the opposition is enraged, this Pokémon hurls itself at the opponent, tackling them forcefully."},{"id":"swsh3.5-37","localId":"37","name":"Galarian Obstagoon","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/37","description":"Its voice is staggering in volume. Obstagoon has a tendency to take on a threatening posture and shout—this move is known as Obstruct."},{"id":"swsh3.5-38","localId":"38","name":"Absol","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/38","description":"The elderly call it the disaster Pokémon and detest it, but interest in its power to predict disasters is on the rise."},{"id":"swsh3.5-39","localId":"39","name":"Purrloin","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/39","description":"It steals things from people just to amuse itself with their frustration. A rivalry exists between this Pokémon and Nickit."},{"id":"swsh3.5-4","localId":"4","name":"Beedrill","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/4","description":"May appear in a swarm. Flies at violent speeds, all the while stabbing with the toxic stinger on its rear."},{"id":"swsh3.5-40","localId":"40","name":"Liepard","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/40","description":"Don't be fooled by its gorgeous fur and elegant figure. This is a moody and vicious Pokémon."},{"id":"swsh3.5-41","localId":"41","name":"Scraggy","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/41","description":"If it locks eyes with you, watch out! Nothing and no one is safe from the reckless headbutts of this troublesome Pokémon."},{"id":"swsh3.5-42","localId":"42","name":"Scrafty","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/42","description":"As halfhearted as this Pokémon's kicks may seem, they pack enough power to shatter Conkeldurr's concrete pillars."},{"id":"swsh3.5-43","localId":"43","name":"Trubbish","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/43","description":"Its favorite places are unsanitary ones. If you leave trash lying around, you could even find one of these Pokémon living in your room."},{"id":"swsh3.5-44","localId":"44","name":"Inkay","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/swsh/swsh3.5/44","description":"It spins while making its luminescent spots flash. These spots allow it to communicate with others by using different patterns of light."},{"id":"swsh3.5-45","localId":"45","name":"Malamar","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":true,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://asset